 "intro_html": "Two Okayama dishes from the Seto Inland Sea, put together: <b>takomeshi</b> — rice cooked with octopus, ginger and dashi — and <b>iidako no nitsuke</b>, baby octopus simmered whole in sweet soy. The rice becomes round onigiri; each one gets a whole glazed baby octopus sitting on top, tentacles draped over the sides and tucked under a strip of nori. Shaping basics (wet hands, salt, gentle pressure) are on the <a href=\"onigiri.html\">onigiri page</a>.",
