  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Put the soy sauce, mirin, sugar and water in the saucepan and bring to a boil.</li><li>Add the octopus, bring back to a boil, then turn down to <b>medium</b>.</li><li>Cover with a drop lid (or a round of baking paper laid on the liquid) and simmer for 20 minutes.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium",
    "label_html": "<span>medium</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-7",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Simmer in sweet soy",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Cover with a drop lid and simmer 20 minutes.",
      "src": "illustrations/baby-octopus-onigiri/7-how1.webp?v=212e05ba0c"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/baby-octopus-onigiri/7.webp?v=82e24f2d68",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 7,
   "part": "Sweet-soy baby octopus",
   "part_id": "part-sweet-soy-baby-octopus",
   "time": "20 min",
   "time_html": "<span>20 min</span>",
   "title": "Simmer in sweet soy",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1.5\">1½ tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Soy sauce"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1.5\">1½ tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Mirin (for the simmer)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Sugar"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"200\">200 ml</span>",
     "name_html": "Water"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Take off the drop lid and turn the heat up to medium-high.</li><li>Spoon the sauce over and roll the octopus around until it's syrupy and they're dark and glossy, 3–5 minutes.</li><li>Off the heat. Leave them in the glaze until the rice is ready.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium-high",
    "label_html": "<span>medium-high</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-8",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Reduce to a glaze",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Lid off, medium-high: spoon the sauce over until syrupy and glossy.",
      "src": "illustrations/baby-octopus-onigiri/8-how1.webp?v=5be23ab85d"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/baby-octopus-onigiri/8.webp?v=a50794cc59",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 8,
   "part": "Sweet-soy baby octopus",
   "part_id": "part-sweet-soy-baby-octopus",
   "time": "3–5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>3–5 min</span>",
   "title": "Reduce to a glaze",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>When the rice is done, scatter the green onion over it and fold it through gently with the paddle, cutting through the rice rather than mashing it.</li><li>Let it cool for a few minutes, until it's warm enough to hold.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-9",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Fold in the green onion",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Fold the green onion through with the paddle — cut, don't mash.",
      "src": "illustrations/baby-octopus-onigiri/9-how1.webp?v=167cd5700a"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/baby-octopus-onigiri/9.webp?v=0d964baf87",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 9,
   "part": "Shape",
   "part_id": "part-shape",
   "time": "~7 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~7 min</span>",
   "title": "Fold in the green onion",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"1\" data-f=\"stalk|stalks\" data-n=\"1\">1 stalk</span>",
     "name_html": "Green onion"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Wet your hands and rub a pinch of salt over your palms.</li><li>Take about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"90\" data-s=\"0\">90 g</span> of takomeshi (a sixth of it) and press it gently into a ball, with octopus pieces all through it.</li><li>Flatten the top and bottom a little between your palms, so it's a thick puck about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"6\" data-s=\"0\">6 cm</span> across that stands on its own.</li><li>Press a shallow dip into the top with your thumb. Repeat for six.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-10",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Shape round onigiri",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Wet, salted hands: press about 90 g into a ball.",
      "src": "illustrations/baby-octopus-onigiri/10-how1.webp?v=447574b092"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Flatten the top and bottom into a thick puck, then press a dip in the top.",
      "src": "illustrations/baby-octopus-onigiri/10-how2.webp?v=6cacb7b0d0"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/baby-octopus-onigiri/10.webp?v=8c92bd7144",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 10,
   "part": "Shape",
   "part_id": "part-shape",
   "time": "~10 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~10 min</span>",
   "title": "Shape round onigiri",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "a pinch per onigiri",
     "name_html": "Salt (for your hands)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Brush a little glaze into the dip and sit one glazed octopus in it, head up, tentacles draped down over the edge.</li><li>Wrap a nori strip around the side of the onigiri, over the tentacle tips, so it holds them in place; the end of the strip sticks to itself.</li><li>Brush a little more glaze over each octopus.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-11",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Octopus on top, nori belt",
